OCR models (downloaded on demand, not bundled)
----------------------------------------------

Kimochi does not include any OCR model. When you choose MeikiOCR or Manga OCR,
the app downloads that engine's model files from their upstream location.
Every file is pinned by revision, SHA-256 and size in src-tauri/ocr-models.json.

MeikiOCR models, LGPL-3.0, by rtr46 on Hugging Face:
  - https://huggingface.co/rtr46/meiki.text.detect.v0
    (revision a9cffa4f60cbf72ddb87edf19c6f98a01cd042e6)
  - https://huggingface.co/rtr46/meiki.txt.recognition.v0
    (revision a28cf5874dc2438ebb1c86336be26bcec51e3375)

Manga OCR model, Apache-2.0: https://huggingface.co/kha-white/manga-ocr-base
(revision aa6573bd10b0d446cbf622e29c3e084914df9741).

Comic Text Detector ONNX weights, GPL-3.0, from dmMaze/comic-text-detector,
as distributed by zyddnys/manga-image-translator (GPL-3.0), release
beta-0.2.1:
https://github.com/zyddnys/manga-image-translator/releases/tag/beta-0.2.1


OneOCR (Windows, optional)
--------------------------

Kimochi does not include or redistribute anything from Microsoft for OneOCR.
The OneOCR engine uses oneocr.dll, oneocr.onemodel and onnxruntime.dll that
you supply yourself from your own copy of Windows Snipping Tool (see
docs/ONEOCR.md); your use of those files is governed by Microsoft's terms for
that software. Kimochi ships only its own GPL-3.0-only helper process
(oneocr-worker/), which loads them.


